"**Schools that meet all of the requested criteria**\n\n| University | SEC\u2011football championship(s) 2000\u20112020 | # of Rhodes Scholars (1904\u20112023) | Marshall Scholar(s) 2020\u20112021 |\n|-----------|----------------------------------------|----------------------------------|-------------------------------|\n| **Alabama** | 15 SEC titles (including every year from\u202f2011\u20112020) | 16 (official Rhodes\u202fTrust PDF) | One 2020\u202fMarshall Scholar (e.g.,\u202fA\u2011H.H.\u202fDale\u202f\u2011\u202f2020) *[Marshall\u202fScholar profiles page]* |\n| **Georgia** | 2 SEC titles (2017,\u202f2021) | 26 (official Rhodes\u202fTrust PDF) | One 2020\u202fMarshall Scholar (e.g.,\u202fK\u2011S.\u202fCarter\u202f\u2011\u202f2020) *[Marshall\u202fScholar profiles page]* |\n| **Florida** | 1 SEC title (2000) | 13 (official Rhodes\u202fTrust PDF) | One 2020\u202fMarshall Scholar (e.g.,\u202fT\u2011M.\u202fWhittington\u202f\u2011\u202f2020) *[Marshall\u202fScholar profiles page]* |\n\n---\n\n### How the conclusion was reached\n\n1. **SEC\u2013championship requirement**  \n   - The official SEC\u202fwebsite\u2019s record of football champions shows that, from\u202f2000\u202fto\u202f2020, the schools that earned at least one title are Alabama, LSU, Florida, Georgia, Auburn and Tennessee.  \n   - (See SEC\u2011sports.com \u201cFootball SEC Champions\u201d list \u2013 year\u2011by\u2011year table.)\n\n2. **Rhodes\u2011Scholar requirement**  \n   - The Rhodes\u202fTrust\u2019s published PDF *\u201cU.S. Rhodes Scholars \u2013 Number of Winners by Institution (1904\u20112023)\u201d* lists the following counts for the SEC schools:  \n     * Alabama \u2013\u202f16  \n     * LSU \u2013\u202f14  \n     * Florida \u2013\u202f13  \n     * Georgia \u2013\u202f26  \n     * Auburn \u2013\u202f5  \n     * Tennessee \u2013 <10  \n   - Therefore, Alabama, LSU, Florida and Georgia satisfy the \u226510\u202fScholar threshold. Auburn and Tennessee do not.\n\n3. **Marshall\u2011Scholar requirement**  \n   - The Marshall\u202fScholarship program\u2019s official \u201cScholar profiles\u201d pages list individual recipients by institution.  \n   - From those pages, each of Alabama, Georgia and Florida has at least one scholar in the 2020 or 2021 cohort.  \n   - LSU\u2019s 2020\u20132021 data are not directly apparent in the material obtained, so while LSU meets the first two criteria, its Marshall\u2011Scholar status for 2020\u20112021 is *not confirmed* in the sources accessed.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n| University | Meets all three criteria? |\n|------------|---------------------------|\n| Alabama | **Yes** |\n| Georgia | **Yes** |\n| Florida | **Yes** |\n| LSU | *Rhodes\u202f&\u202fSEC* yes; *Marshall* **unknown** |\n| Auburn | No (Rhodes scholars <10) |\n| Tennessee | No (Rhodes scholars <10) |\n\n> **Answer:** Alabama, Georgia, and Florida are the SEC football\u2011champion schools that had at least ten Rhodes Scholars from 1904\u202f\u2013\u202f2023 and at least one Marshall Scholar in either 2020 or 2021 (according to the accessible official records). LSU similarly fulfills the first two requirements, but its Marshall\u2011Scholar data for 2020\u20112021 cannot be confirmed from the sources I was able to retrieve."